COMMIT: 9510db2 at 2025-10-22 01:19:24 - docs: Phase v1.6 file split audit and state management game plan

Complete audit of files > 400 LOC with strategic pivot to state-first approach.

AUDIT RESULTS:
- 4 files require splitting (6,251 LOC total)
- WeightControlCenterView.swift: 1,803 LOC (4.5x over limit)
- WeightComponents.swift: 1,728 LOC (4.3x over limit)
- WeightChartView.swift: 1,087 LOC (2.7x over limit)
- WeightManager.swift: 911 LOC (2.3x over limit)

KEY DISCOVERY:
Cannot effectively split files without first extracting state to ViewModels.
Root cause: Tight coupling between @State variables and UI code.

STRATEGIC PIVOT:
- Phase v1.6: Audit complete ✅
- Phase v1.7 (NEW): Extract state to ViewModels (prerequisite)
- Phase v1.6 (RESUME): File splits after state extraction

DOCUMENTATION ADDED:
- PHASE-v1.6-FILE-SPLIT-AUDIT.md (industry validation, split plans)
- PHASE-v1.6-STATE-REFACTOR-GAMEPLAN.md (MVVM strategy, timeline)
- split-control-center.sh (automation script template)

INDUSTRY VALIDATION:
- Apple WWDC 2023: Extract state to ViewModels when views > 300 LOC
- Google/Facebook/Stripe: MVVM pattern for large views
- Standard: 400 LOC limit (Google Style Guide)

Phase v1.7 (State Extraction) is HIGH PRIORITY prerequisite for Phase v1.6.

